{"name":"Countryside","hex":"#a4a404","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"countryside","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area located outside of towns and cities; an area that is not urban or suburban; a rural area.","Such part of a larger area."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/countryside"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rural area","blocks":[{"text":"A rural area, also known as the country or countryside, is a geographic area that is located outside towns and cities. Typical rural areas have a low population density and small settlements. Agricultural areas and areas with forestry are typically described as rural, as well as other areas lacking substantial development. Different countries have varying definitions of rural for statistical and administrative purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Joshua_Shaw_-_%27View_in_the_Pennsylvania_Countryside%27%2C_1823.JPG/330px-Joshua_Shaw_-_%27View_in_the_Pennsylvania_Countryside%27%2C_1823.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rural_area","wikidata":"Q175185"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg/500px-Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg/1280px-Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg/500px-Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Westminster, Vermont","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Indiana-rural-road.jpg/500px-Indiana-rural-road.jpg?utm_sour